@@ -17,6 +17,8 @@ All notable codex-tui changes are recorded here.
 
 ### Audit hardening
 
+- Heap-own the interactive future at the CLI boundary to prevent native Windows debug startup stack overflow, without increasing thread stacks or weakening CLI exit/state checks. Retain help, invalid-usage, missing-backend, benchmark and version process controls.
+
 - Route interactive SIGTERM/SIGHUP/SIGINT through terminal restoration and the existing bounded final save; retain distinct raw-Ctrl+C and Drawer cases. Enable Tokio's existing signal feature without changing dependency versions or the lockfile.
 - Bind Forge stdout/stderr readers to command cancellation/deadlines instead of detached tasks; cover repeated descendant-held pipe timeouts, caller cancellation and large healthy output.
 - Rebase small Registry deltas from current inputs before installing a planning result, including membership and shared-worktree collisions; preserve operator/authority fences and a 64-card delta budget. Keep continuous 5k Board fixtures and cross-view controls in the existing PTY workflow.
diff --git a/docs/guides/troubleshooting.md b/docs/guides/troubleshooting.md
index 191b620..5a97103 100644
--- a/docs/guides/troubleshooting.md
+++ b/docs/guides/troubleshooting.md
@@ -43,6 +43,8 @@ PTY children remain owned by a kill-and-reap guard through initialization and th
 
 Catchable Unix process signals (SIGTERM, SIGHUP and SIGINT) enter the ordinary interactive shutdown path. Raw terminal mode, alternate screen and cursor are restored before the final bounded state save; a save failure remains an error. Raw Ctrl+C input and OS SIGINT are separate cases. SIGKILL and a disconnected physical terminal cannot be made restorable by an application. These handlers are not installed for headless subcommands.
 
+The interactive future is heap-owned at the CLI boundary so native Windows debug builds do not carry it in the entry stack frame. Help, version and invalid usage still run without a TTY, backend or state writes; no larger thread stack is required.
+
